More consequentially, all15 choices of2 out of the preregistered6 points[0,.1,.2,1,3,4] were tested without compression.31 of105 pairs reverse strict ranking relative to standard Gaussian MMD. Example: allocation[0,1] has native .5350329429 and MMD .6682947616; allocation[0,4] has native .5642294304 and MMD .3189697182. Therefore the unequal-count mismatch is not only a harmless common rescaling. No extra fixture search was performed. Raw inputs, selected indices, all native scores, references and reversals are retained.

Scope: API/estimand mismatch for unequal groups, not a measured false-positive excess or power loss. Under valid exchangeability a permutation test may calibrate a different statistic. Published balanced comparisons are not refuted. Do not silently apply a scalar correction to unequal counts, nor claim a new algorithm from repairing a standard weighted mean. Native cttc.signed_matrix_sum assumes +/-1 and adds K_ii directly; passing arbitrary 1/a,-1/b weights to that Cython function would not implement the corrected quadratic form. A future corrected implementation must compute fully weighted diagonals/cross terms or an independently verified equivalent.

Decision: retain the native sources as diagnostic baselines; use balanced counts for the next cost-only comparison. Do not compare raw CTT statistic amplitudes across compression levels. Unequal-count extensions require explicit estimand normalization plus independent calibration/power assessment before scientific comparison. Separate external-pilot bandwidth source review resolves the previous suspicion for the author's synthetic iid benchmark: pilot is separate, so no observed bandwidth validity defect is established.
